<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70460" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέπους</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποδος</span>, ὁ, once in <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> in pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέποδες καλῆς
		Ἁλοσύδνης,</span> of seals, prob. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>children</i> of H., <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.404
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1502.36
			</span></i>: so in later Poets, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀθάνατοι δὲ καλεῦνται ἑοὶ νέποδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					17.25
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γοργοφόνοι νέποδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cleon Sic.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				389.28
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ Κεῖος Ὑλλίχου νέπους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					77
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.1745
			</span></i>: also expld. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νε-</span> (for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νη-</span> privat.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πούς,</span>
			<i>the footless ones,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Apion
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				Apollon.
				<u>Lex.</u>
			</span></i>, and from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέω</span> (A), 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηξί-ποδες</span>
			, <i>web-footed,</i> ibid., <i><span class="en">
				<u>Et.Gud.</u>
				405.49
			</span></i>: hence in later Poets, of <i>fish,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θαλασσαίων μυνδότεροι νεπόδων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					260
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Al.</u>
				468
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				485
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.11
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Satyr.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				11.60
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕκαστά τε φῦλα
				νεπούδων</span> is f.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ap.</u>
				78
			</span></i>.</div>
